# Arrol-Johnston 10/12 hp dogcart, c.1902-1905.
#
# The Glasgow-built Arrol-Johnston dogcart: a two-cylinder car with a
# rear-entrance body. Arrol-Johnston made an estimated 700 cars in 1907 and
# 1,150 in 1913. SA 88 is a c.1904-05 car by its Aberdeen plate and the
# model's end date.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrol-Johnston
#
# Dimensions 3.1 x 1.6 x 1.8 m, wheelbase 2.1 m. All four are estimates
# measured from the photographs; no published dimension box was found.
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of SA 88. No front
# three-quarter of SA 88 exists in Commons; the front view is the detail
# image. The limitation is recorded. The 1905 12/15 hp, the 1905 TT racer
# and the 1902 ST 52 dogcart were examined and excluded as different models.
#
# Colours: grade (d), no period UK document consulted. Black, Dark Green,
# Maroon and Grey are plain colour names. Weights 3, 2, 1, 1, total 7,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 50 km/h. Comfort 18/357, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 18. Class 3.
# Dates c.1902-1905 production, road tail staggered 1914-1916.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/arrol-johnston-10-12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/arrol-johnston-10-12.dae. References:
# citycars/references/arrol-johnston-10-12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: SA 88 is modelled as the photographed dogcart from its
# true side. No front three-quarter of SA 88 exists; the front follows the detail
# image. Preserving the side-photograph proportions at the brief's wheelbase
# gives a model length of 3.93 m, not the brief's 3.1 m estimate.


obj=citycar
name=ArrolJohnston10_12(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1902
intro_month=1
retire_year=1916
retire_month=6
speed=50
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=18
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=357

